        <item>
            <title>2.26.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 17:08:03 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>108</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.26.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Answer an AskUserQuestion from your phone.** When Claude asks a multiple-choice question, the push now shows the choices as buttons instead of the raw tool input. Pick an option, tap Send, and the question resolves on the Mac — single- and multi-select both work. Previously the question was readable on the phone but could only be answered by walking back to the Mac.

### Bug Fixes

- **Canopy now notices when its connection to the relay dies silently.** A half-open socket reports nothing, so the relay kept accepting messages for a Mac that could no longer hear them — the phone showed them as sent while nothing arrived. Measured at 47 minutes on an idle Mac. A periodic ping now detects the loss and reconnects on its own clock.
- **A reply or permission decision from the phone now reports what actually happened.** "Sent" used to mean only that the relay had written to a socket. It now means the Mac received the message and acted on it; a session that has closed, a shim that is not running, or a request that is no longer waiting comes back with the Mac's own reason instead of a silent success.
]]></description>
